Trademarks
----------
RuneScape is a trademark of Jagex Ltd. Alto is an independent project. It is
not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by Jagex Ltd. The name RuneScape
is used only to identify the game the software is compatible with (nominative
use). Alto contains no Jagex code, game assets, cache data or shaders. The
game cache, which you must supply yourself, is Jagex's data and is never
committed to this repository.

Components and origins
----------------------

1. Client, engine and tools (tools/client910, tools/native910, tools/perf,
   tools/refactor)
   Original work, Copyright (c) 2026 robert dennis, under the MIT License.
   The client is written as our own engine. Its behaviour is checked against
   recordings of observable behaviour (packet bytes and tables, variable state,
   script stacks, draw output) committed as plain data under
   tools/client910/fixtures and tools/native910/tests/fixtures. Those
   recordings are test data for interoperability, not source code.

2. Modern renderer (tools/client910/crates/rs910-render-modern)
   The renderer reimplements, in our own WGSL and Rust, rendering techniques
   used by later game clients (cascaded sun shadows, ambient occlusion,
   physically based lighting with image-based reflections, screen-space and
   volumetric atmosphere effects, water shading and a bloom and tone-map
   chain). The techniques are widely published. No shader source text, binary
   or asset of the original game is included in this repository.

3. Rust dependencies
   The Rust workspace (tools/Cargo.toml, lockfile tools/Cargo.lock) depends on
   open-source crates from crates.io, among them wgpu, winit, cpal, tokio,
   glam, bytemuck, anyhow, thiserror, log, clap and serde_json. Each is under
   its own licence, mostly MIT, Apache-2.0 or both. The full list with the
   licence text of every crate is in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

4. Dependency notices
   THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md is generated from the Rust lockfiles: run
   `python3 tools/licenses.py` after changing a lockfile (`--check` reports a
   stale file). The private server and its dependencies are not distributed.

5. Data formats
   The cache, JS5 and interface formats that Alto reads and writes are
   documented by the community, in particular by the OpenRS2 project
   (https://www.openrs2.org). No code from those projects is included unless
   listed above.
